  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Quiet Instrument",
    "overview": "Psycray is an internal tool for operators: sales and business-development people who sit with it for long sessions, research a company, read the evidence and decide whether to pursue it. The interface behaves like a well-made measuring instrument. The chrome is near-monochrome zinc, so the few saturated marks on screen carry meaning: deep indigo says \"act here\", and emerald, amber and red give the fit verdict. Everything else stays out of the way.\n\nDensity is moderate and calm. Screens use dense type (14px body, 13px mono) on a generous container, with 1px hairlines rather than shadows separating surfaces. The system rejects the category default of gradient hero cards, glowing stat tiles and decorative charts; a number appears only when it was measured, and it is set in tabular figures.\n\nThe brand is the word \"Psycray\" in Geist semibold. No logo, wordmark or brand color exists, so none is invented.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Zinc neutrals in both themes; one deep-indigo accent reserved for primary actions, focus and the active nav icon.",
      "Fit tiers in semantic color: emerald High, amber Moderate, red Low, slate Needs Review, always as a tinted badge with a dot.",
      "Flat surfaces separated by a single 1px border; shadows only on overlays.",
      "Geist for UI, Geist Mono for domains and URLs, tabular numerals for every metric.",
      "Theme follows the OS, remembers an explicit choice, and is applied before first paint."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Meaningful Saturation Rule",
        "body": "Chrome is monochrome. A saturated color on screen is either indigo (act here, focus, where you are) or a verdict hue. Nothing decorative is colored.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Verdict Palette Rule",
        "body": "Emerald, amber and red mean High, Moderate and Low Fit (and success, warning, error). Never use them for decoration, and never show Needs Review or \"unknown\" in a verdict hue; unknown is not failure.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Semantic Token Rule",
        "body": "Components reference semantic tokens only, so light and dark stay in step. A raw `bg-indigo-600` or `text-zinc-500` in a component is a bug.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Metric Rule",
        "body": "Every number that is compared or scored (score, `20 / 20`, counts) uses `tabular-nums`, so columns of figures align.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Machine Identifier Rule",
        "body": "Domains, URLs and IDs are set in Geist Mono; human language never is.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Hairline Rule",
        "body": "Containers are separated by exactly one 1px border in the hairline token. No card shadows, no double borders, no colored side stripes.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** reference semantic tokens (`bg-card`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-success-border`) so both themes stay correct.",
      "**Do** keep indigo to the primary action, focus rings and the active nav icon.",
      "**Do** show fit tiers with `FitBadge`: soft verdict fill, a dot, and the tier written out.",
      "**Do** separate surfaces with one 1px hairline and 14px corners; keep controls at 8px.",
      "**Do** set domains and URLs in Geist Mono at 13px, and every compared number in tabular figures.",
      "**Do** add new pages to `src/config/navigation.ts` with a one-line description; the header reads its title from there.",
      "**Do** give every icon-only control an aria-label and a tooltip.",
      "**Do** honor reduced motion; the global rule already shortens transitions and animations to 0.01 ms."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** put shadows on cards or other in-flow surfaces; shadows are for overlays.",
      "**Don't** use emerald, amber or red for anything except verdicts and status, and don't color Needs Review or unknown data as failure.",
      "**Don't** use gradient hero cards, glowing stat tiles or decorative charts.",
      "**Don't** invent a logo or a brand color for Psycray; the brand is the word.",
      "**Don't** use raw Tailwind palette classes (`bg-indigo-600`, `text-zinc-500`) inside components.",
      "**Don't** present mock data as real; keep the amber \"Mock data\" badge visible whenever the API runs in mock mode."
    ]
  }
}